3. Provided the SingleValueComponent through the components prop
4. Set up basic required props for the Select component
5. Removed all the complex styling props and let react-select handle them internally
6. Used the proper component composition pattern that react-select expects

This approach should work better because:
1. It uses the proper React-Select component hierarchy
2. It lets React-Select handle all the internal prop passing
3. It matches how the SingleValueComponent is meant to be used based on the source code
4. It provides the correct context for the SingleValueComponent

The error should be resolved now as we're using the proper component structure that React-Select expects.

